  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "This was great. The only real change I made to it was using frozen corn in place of the green peppers. I thought the corn went well with the beans and tomatoes. The flavor of the dish was excellent and it was very hearty. I did sprinkle a little bit of shredded cheddar on top with the mozzarella for color. I could also see throwing leftover cubed chicken or cooked ground beef in with this as well."
    },
    {
      "text": "Yum! I really, really enjoyed this delicious, filling dish! I agree, however, that a little bit of salt is needed."
    },
    {
      "text": "Overall very good, but the cooking time wasn't long enough to cook the rice completely - I used brown rice instead of white, so this may have been part of the problem. Also, the recipe needs a fair amount of salt added. I don't like mushrooms, so I left those out and added one zucchini and one yellow squash instead."
    },
    {
      "text": "I added a little more of each seasoning & I did add some salt as well. I also substituted pepper jack cheese. I will definetly be making this again & again!"
    },
    {
      "text": "I used Lundford Wild/Brown Rice and shredded pepper jack cheese. For me, this was a great mix of rice and beans with the right amount of spicy without too much HOT."
    },
    {
      "text": "This recipe was pretty good. In the future I will add shredded chicken and more tomatoes."
    },
    {
      "text": "I doubled up on all spices and added a little salt."
    }
  ],
